      "text": "758,440.\n</think>\n\nSure, let's solve the multiplication problem step by step.\n\n**Question:**  \nWhat is the product of **760** and **998**?\n\n**Solution:**\n\nTo find the product of **760** and **998**, we'll use the standard multiplication method.\n\n1. **Multiply 760 by 8 (the ones place digit of 998):**\n   \n   \\[\n   760 \\times 8 = 6,080\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 760 by 90 (the tens place digit of 998):**\n   \n   \\[\n   760 \\times 90 = 68,400\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 760 by 900 (the hundreds place digit of 998):**\n   \n   \\[\n   760 \\times 900 = 684,000\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum all the results:**\n   \n   \\[\n   6,080 + 68,400 + 684,000 = 758,480\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer:**  \n\\[\n\\boxed{758,\\!480}\n\\]",
