      "text": "252,240.\n</think>\n\nSure, let's solve the multiplication problem step by step.\n\n**Question:**  \nWhat is the product of **720** and **348**?\n\n**Solution:**\n\nTo find the product of 720 and 348, we'll break down the multiplication into simpler parts based on the place values of the digits in 348.\n\n1. **Multiply 720 by the ones place digit of 348 (8):**\n   \n   \\[\n   720 \\times 8 = 5,\\!760\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 720 by the tens place digit of 348 (4), remembering to shift one position to the left (since it's the tens place):**\n   \n   \\[\n   720 \\times 40 = 28,\\!800\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 720 by the hundreds place digit of 348 (3), shifting two positions to the left (since it's the hundreds place):**\n   \n   \\[\n   720 \\times 300 = 216,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add all the results together to get the final product:**\n   \n   \\[\n   5,\\!760 + 28,\\!800 + 216,\\!000 = 250,\\!560\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer:**  \n\\[\n\\boxed{250,\\!560}\n\\]",
