      "text": "129,  604 multiplied by 215 equals 129,  604 \u00d7 215 = 129,  604 \u00d7 200 = 120,800; 604 \u00d7 10 = 6,040; 604 \u00d7 5 = 3,020. Adding them up: 120,800 + 6,040 = 126,840; 126,840 + 3,020 = 129,860. So, the final product is 129,860.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **604** and **215**, we'll break down the multiplication step by step.\n\n### Step 1: Multiply 604 by 5 (the ones place of 215)\n\\[\n604 \\times 5 = 3,\\!020\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Multiply 604 by 10 (the tens place of 215)\n\\[\n604 \\times 10 = 6,\\!040\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Multiply 604 by 200 (the hundreds place of 215)\n\\[\n604 \\times 200 = 120,\\!800\n\\]\n\n### Step 4: Sum All the Results\n\\[\n3,\\!020 + 6,\\!040 + 120,\\!800 = 129,\\!860\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer:\n\\[\n\\boxed{129,\\!860}\n\\]",
