      "text": "82,500.\n</think>\n\nSure, let's solve the multiplication problem step by step.\n\n**Question:**  \nWhat is the product of **750** and **110**?\n\n**Solution:**\n\nTo find the product of 750 and 110, we can break down the multiplication into simpler steps.\n\n1. **Multiply 750 by 0 (the ones place digit of 110):**\n   \\[\n   750 \\times 0 = 0\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 750 by 10 (the tens place digit of 110):**\n   \\[\n   750 \\times 10 = 7,500\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 750 by 100 (the hundreds place digit of 110):**\n   \\[\n   750 \\times 100 = 75,000\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum all the results:**\n   \\[\n   0 + 7,500 + 75,000 = 82,500\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer:**  \n\\[\n\\boxed{82,\\!500}\n\\]",
