      "text": "190,  1470 + 18,900 + 168,000 = 188,  1470 + 18,900 = 20,370; 20,370 + 168,000 = 188,370\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **210** and **897**, we'll follow a step-by-step multiplication process:\n\n### Step 1: Multiply 210 by each digit of 897\n\n1. **Ones place (7):**\n   \\[\n   210 \\times 7 = 1470\n   \\]\n   \n2. **Tens place (9):**\n   \\[\n   210 \\times 90 = 18900\n   \\]\n   \n3. **Hundreds place (8):**\n   \\[\n   210 \\times 800 = 168000\n   \\]\n\n### Step 2: Sum all the results\n\n\\[\n1470 + 18900 + 168000 = 188370\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{188370}\n\\]",
