      "text": "680800 + 8510 + 5106 = 694,416\n</think>\n\nSure, let's solve the multiplication problem step by step.\n\n**Question:**  \nWhat is the product of **851** and **816**?\n\n**Solution:**\n\nTo find the product of **851** and **816**, we'll use the standard multiplication method, breaking it down into simpler steps.\n\n1. **Multiply 851 by 6 (the ones place of 816):**\n   \n   \\[\n   851 \\times 6 = 5106\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 851 by 10 (the tens place of 816):**\n   \n   \\[\n   851 \\times 10 = 8510\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 851 by 800 (the hundreds place of 816):**\n   \n   \\[\n   851 \\times 800 = 680800\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add all the results together:**\n   \n   \\[\n   5106 + 8510 + 680800 = 694416\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer:**  \n\\[\n\\boxed{694416}\n\\]",
