      "text": "74,668.\n</think>\n\nSure, let's solve the multiplication problem step by step.\n\n**Question:**  \nWhat is the product of **274** and **272**?\n\n**Solution:**\n\nTo find the product of **274** and **272**, we'll use the standard multiplication method.\n\n1. **Multiply 274 by 2 (the ones place digit of 272):**\n   \\[\n   274 \\times 2 = 548\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 274 by 70 (the tens place digit of 272):**\n   \\[\n   274 \\times 70 = 19,\\!180\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 274 by 200 (the hundreds place digit of 272):**\n   \\[\n   274 \\times 200 = 54,\\!800\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add all the results together:**\n   \\[\n   548 + 19,\\!180 + 54,\\!800 = 74,\\!528\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer:**  \n\\[\n\\boxed{74,\\!528}\n\\]",
