      "text": "251,250.\n</think>\n\nSure, let's solve the multiplication problem step by step.\n\n**Question:**  \nWhat is the product of **335** and **750**?\n\n**Solution:**\n\nTo find the product of **335** and **750**, we'll break down the multiplication into simpler parts based on the place values of the digits in **750**.\n\n1. **Multiply 335 by 0 (the ones place digit of 750):**\n   \\[\n   335 \\times 0 = 0\n   \\]\n   \n2. **Multiply 335 by 50 (the tens place digit of 750):**\n   \\[\n   335 \\times 50 = 16,\\!750\n   \\]\n   \n3. **Multiply 335 by 700 (the hundreds place digit of 750):**\n   \\[\n   335 \\times 700 = 234,\\!500\n   \\]\n   \n4. **Sum all the results:**\n   \\[\n   0 + 16,\\!750 + 234,\\!500 = 251,\\!250\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer:**  \n\\[\n\\boxed{251,\\!250}\n\\]",
