batch_outputs:  [['\n\n# Solution:\n\nTo find the product of **564** and **111**, we can break down the multiplication step by step.\n\n1. **Multiply 564 by 1 (the ones place digit of 111):**\n   \n   \\[\n   564 \\times 1 = 564\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 564 by 10 (the tens place digit of 111):**\n   \n   \\[\n   564 \\times 10 = 5640\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 564 by 100 (the hundreds place digit of 111):**\n   \n   \\[\n   564 \\times 100 = 56400\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum all the results:**\n   \n   \\[\n   564 + 5640 + 56400 = 62264\n   \\]\n\nSo, the final computed product is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{62264}\n\\]', '62264.\n']]
