batch_outputs:  [['\n\n# Answer:\n\nThe product of **684** and **119** is **81,396**.\n\n# Step-by-Step Explanation:\n\nTo find the product of **684** and **119**, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Break down the multiplication:**\n   \n   - Multiply **684** by each digit of **119** separately.\n   \n2. **Multiply by the ones place:**\n   \n   - **684 × 9 = 6,156**\n\n3. **Multiply by the tens place:**\n   \n   - **684 × 10 = 6,840**\n\n4. **Multiply by the hundreds place:**\n   \n   - **684 × 100 = 68,400**\n\n5. **Add all the results together:**\n   \n   - **6,156 + 6,840 = 12,996**\n   - **12,996 + 68,400 = 81,396**\n\n6. **Final Answer:**\n   \n   - **684 × 119 = 81,396**\n\n\\boxed{81,\\!396}', '684 × 119 = 81,  684 × 100 = 68,400; 684 × 10 = 6,840; 684 × 9 = 6,156. Adding them up: 68,400 + 6,840 = 75,240; 75,240 + 6,156 = 81,396.\n']]
