      "text": "698,  6060.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **894** and **790**, we'll follow a step-by-step multiplication process:\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Multiplication\nWe can break down the multiplication into smaller, more manageable parts by considering each digit of the second number (790) separately.\n\n1. **Multiply by the ones place digit (0):**\n   \\[\n   894 \\times 0 = 0\n   \\]\n   \n2. **Multiply by the tens place digit (9):**\n   \\[\n   894 \\times 9 = 8046\n   \\]\n   Since this is the tens place, we'll add a zero at the end:\n   \\[\n   8046 \\times 10 = 80460\n   \\]\n   \n3. **Multiply by the hundreds place digit (7):**\n   \\[\n   894 \\times 7 = 6258\n   \\]\n   Since this is the hundreds place, we'll add two zeros at the end:\n   \\[\n   6258 \\times 100 = 625800\n   \\]\n\n### Step 2: Sum All the Results\nNow, add all the partial products together:\n\\[\n0 + 80460 + 625800 = 706260\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\\[\n\\boxed{706260}\n\\]",
