      "text": "429,  464.\n</think>\n\nSure, let's solve the multiplication problem step by step.\n\n**Question:**  \nWhat is the product of **794** and **536**?\n\n**Solution:**\n\nTo find the product of **794** and **536**, we'll use the standard multiplication algorithm. Here's a step-by-step breakdown:\n\n1. **Multiply 794 by 6 (the ones place digit of 536):**\n   \\[\n   794 \\times 6 = 4,\\!764\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 794 by 30 (the tens place digit of 536):**\n   \\[\n   794 \\times 30 = 23,\\!820\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 794 by 500 (the hundreds place digit of 536):**\n   \\[\n   794 \\times 500 = 397,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add all the results together:**\n   \\[\n   4,\\!764 + 23,\\!820 + 397,\\!000 = 425,\\!584\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer:**  \n\\[\n\\boxed{425,\\!584}\n\\]",
